# Independent security review pack

::summary
`runIndependentSecurityReview()` is the in-repo independent review: a separate probe module that drives the public HTTP surface and kernel invariants. It is not a substitute for a third-party firm's signed report.
::

| ID | Title | Severity | Gate |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| SEC-01 | Unauthenticated search is rejected | critical | HTTP `/v1/search` without a bearer token returns 403 |
| SEC-02 | Restricted documents do not leak through search | critical | An editor on a public space cannot retrieve a restricted document hit |
| SEC-03 | Agents cannot approve their own changesets | critical | `self_approval` |
| SEC-04 | Untrusted payloads cannot grant privileges | high | `policy` on injected `grant` |
| SEC-05 | Scripted SVG is quarantined | high | `readAsset` refuses `image/svg+xml` with a script |

Evidence: `test/enterprise-security-review.test.ts` requires every finding `passed`.
